{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Given the `root` of a binary search tree and two numbers `low` and `high`, remove every node whose value is outside `[low, high]`, keeping the relative structure of the rest. Return the root of the trimmed tree (it may be a different node)."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/d899af90-22ec-4e27-9316-f14eb95ec76b.svg",
      "alt": "The tree 3, 0, 4, null, 2, null, null, 1 trimmed to the range 1 to 3. Node 0 is too small, so it is replaced by its trimmed right subtree, 2 with child 1. Node 4 is too big, so it is replaced by its trimmed left subtree, which is empty. The result is 3, 2, null, 1.",
      "width": 764,
      "height": 527,
      "scene": {
