    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "root = [1, 0, 2], low = 1, high = 2                    ->  [1, null, 2]\nroot = [3, 0, 4, null, 2, null, null, 1], low = 1, high = 3  ->  [3, 2, null, 1]\nroot = [5, 3, 8], low = 6, high = 9                    ->  [8]"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Look at one node. If it's **too small**, then everything in its left subtree is even smaller — throw the node and its whole left side away, and the answer is the trimmed **right** subtree. If it's **too big**, mirror that: the answer is the trimmed **left** subtree. If it's **in range**, keep it and trim both children."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Collect the kept values, rebuild"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Gather every value in the range in pre-order and insert them into a new BST. Pre-order keeps each parent before its children, so the rebuilt tree has the same shape the trimmed tree would."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function trimBST(root, low, high) {\n  const kept = [];\n  const walk = (node) => {\n    if (node === null) return;\n    if (node.val >= low && node.val <= high) kept.push(node.val);   // pre-order\n    walk(node.left);\n    walk(node.right);\n  };\n  walk(root);\n  const insert = (node, val) => {\n    if (node === null) return new TreeNode(val);\n    if (val < node.val) node.left = insert(node.left, val);\n    else node.right = insert(node.right, val);\n    return node;\n  };\n  let result = null;\n  for (const v of kept) result = insert(result, v);\n  return result;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def trim_bst(root, low, high):\n    kept = []\n\n    def walk(node):\n        if node is None:\n            return\n        if low <= node.val <= high:\n            kept.append(node.val)         # pre-order\n        walk(node.left)\n        walk(node.right)\n\n    def insert(node, val):\n        if node is None:\n            return TreeNode(val)\n        if val < node.val:\n            node.left = insert(node.left, val)\n        else:\n            node.right = insert(node.right, val)\n        return node\n\n    walk(root)\n    result = None\n    for v in kept:\n        result = insert(result, v)\n    return result"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "TreeNode trimBST(TreeNode root, int low, int high) {\n    List<Integer> kept = new ArrayList<>();\n    walk(root, low, high, kept);\n    TreeNode result = null;\n    for (int v : kept) result = insert(result, v);\n    return result;\n}\n\nvoid walk(TreeNode node, int low, int high, List<Integer> kept) {\n    if (node == null) return;\n    if (node.val >= low && node.val <= high) kept.add(node.val);   // pre-order\n    walk(node.left, low, high, kept);\n    walk(node.right, low, high, kept);\n}\n\nTreeNode insert(TreeNode node, int val) {\n    if (node == null) return new TreeNode(val);\n    if (val < node.val) node.left = insert(node.left, val);\n    else node.right = insert(node.right, val);\n    return node;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "void walk(TreeNode* node, int low, int high, vector<int>& kept) {\n    if (node == nullptr) return;\n    if (node->val >= low && node->val <= high) kept.push_back(node->val);   // pre-order\n    walk(node->left, low, high, kept);\n    walk(node->right, low, high, kept);\n}\n\nTreeNode* insert(TreeNode* node, int val) {\n    if (node == nullptr) return new TreeNode(val);\n    if (val < node->val) node->left = insert(node->left, val);\n    else node->right = insert(node->right, val);\n    return node;\n}\n\nTreeNode* trimBST(TreeNode* root, int low, int high) {\n    vector<int> kept;\n    walk(root, low, high, kept);\n    TreeNode* result = nullptr;\n    for (int v : kept) result = insert(result, v);\n    return result;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n·h)** — n inserts, each walking a path — and **space O(n)** for the list and the new nodes."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Recursion that skips whole sides"
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "trim-bst",
      "caption": "Too small: return the trimmed right side. Too big: the trimmed left side. In range: keep it."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function trimBST(root, low, high) {\n  if (root === null) return null;\n  if (root.val < low) return trimBST(root.right, low, high);    // root and its left side are too small\n  if (root.val > high) return trimBST(root.left, low, high);    // root and its right side are too big\n  root.left = trimBST(root.left, low, high);\n  root.right = trimBST(root.right, low, high);\n  return root;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def trim_bst(root, low, high):\n    if root is None:\n        return None\n    if root.val < low:\n        return trim_bst(root.right, low, high)   # root and its left side are too small\n    if root.val > high:\n        return trim_bst(root.left, low, high)    # root and its right side are too big\n    root.left = trim_bst(root.left, low, high)\n    root.right = trim_bst(root.right, low, high)\n    return root"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "TreeNode trimBST(TreeNode root, int low, int high) {\n    if (root == null) return null;\n    if (root.val < low) return trimBST(root.right, low, high);     // root and its left side are too small\n    if (root.val > high) return trimBST(root.left, low, high);     // root and its right side are too big\n    root.left = trimBST(root.left, low, high);\n    root.right = trimBST(root.right, low, high);\n    return root;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "TreeNode* trimBST(TreeNode* root, int low, int high) {\n    if (root == nullptr) return nullptr;\n    if (root->val < low) return trimBST(root->right, low, high);   // root and its left side are too small\n    if (root->val > high) return trimBST(root->left, low, high);   // root and its right side are too big\n    root->left = trimBST(root->left, low, high);\n    root->right = trimBST(root->right, low, high);\n    return root;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(h).** Every kept node is visited once, and discarded subtrees are often skipped without being looked at."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "Collect the kept values, rebuild",
          "time": "O(n·h)",
          "timeWhy": "**n** inserts into the new tree, each walking a path of up to **h** nodes.",
          "space": "O(n)",
          "spaceWhy": "The **list of values** and the new nodes."
        },
        {
          "approach": "Recursion that skips whole sides",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "Each kept node is visited **once**; out-of-range sides are often **skipped whole**.",
          "space": "O(h)",
          "spaceWhy": "Recursion **as deep as the tree**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**The root is removed** — the answer is a node from deeper down.",
        "**Nothing is in range** — return null.",
        "**Everything is in range** — the tree comes back unchanged.",
        "**low = high** — at most one node survives."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Range Sum of BST** — the same three-way decision, adding instead of cutting (Pattern 1).",
        "**Delete all nodes below k** — trim with high = +∞.",
        "**Count nodes in a range** — skip sides the same way and count."
      ]
    }
  ],
